  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $517M in contracts in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 96.8% year over year. NASA made 684 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $756K. Historical context shows much larger budgets in recent full fiscal years, including $16.1B in FY26 and $15.8B in FY25. Research and development in the physical, engineering, and life sciences is the largest category this year at $277M. NASA continues to buy specialized air transport, construction, facilities support, and engineering and computer services, but current-year totals are partial. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY received the largest single share of FY2027 to date obligations at $128M. The Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory received $85.3M and BLUE ORIGIN, LLC received $46.1M. The contrast between the FY2027 to date total and prior full-year totals illustrates that current figures represent a partial fiscal year. Readers should treat FY2027 to date as interim contract obligations rather than a full-year sum.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has NASA spending changed this fiscal year?",
        "body": "NASA obligated $517M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 96.8% year over year. NASA obligated $16.1B in FY26 and $15.8B in FY25, showing the FY2027 to date total is much smaller than recent full fiscal years. The FY2027 to date number is a partial fiscal year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are NASA's top contract categories and who receives the largest awards?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the top category at $277M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is second at $94.4M, and Industrial Building Construction is third at $31.5M. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY leads vendors at $128M, followed by THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC at $85.3M and BLUE ORIGIN, LLC at $46.1M."
      }
    ]
